***** Arguments *****

#!/bin/bash

echo "Hello $1"

You may pass any name in first argument

$0 -> Script name or path -> ./greet.sh
$1 -> First argument -> Adnan

--------------------------------------------------

#!/bin/bash

NAME=$1
AGE=$2

echo "My name is $NAME"
echo "My age is $AGE"

You may change the Name and Age in arguments

NAME=$1 stores the first argument in the variable NAME.
AGE=$2 stores the second argument in the variable AGE.
echo displays the values.

-------------------------------------------------------

#!/bin/bash

echo "Script name: $0"
echo "Total arguments: $#"
echo "First argument: $1"
echo "Second argument: $2"

You may pass the multiple arguments, the Total arguments number will change

$# — count the arguments

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#!/bin/bash

echo "All names: $@"

You may pass unlimited arguments

$@ — use all arguments

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The important argument symbols

Symbol   Meaning                                Example
$0       Script name or path                    ./greet.sh
$1       First argument                         Adnan
$2       Second argument                        28
$3       Third argument                         Pune
$#       Number of arguments                    3
$@       All arguments, kept as separate words  All supplied inputs
$?       Exit status of the previous command    0 usually means success
